      "status": "READY_FOR_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW",
      "literalGroups": [
        {
          "group": "prompt_ordered_answers_key",
          "literal": {
            "prompt": "Зачем после смены печатных форм протирают резиновое полотно растворителем?",
            "answers": [
              "Чтобы проверить совмещение цветных форм по меткам",
              "Чтобы изменить количество краски на участках листа",
              "Чтобы удалить след предыдущего изображения",
              "Чтобы закрепить краску перед обрезкой"
            ],
            "correctIndex": 2
          },
          "literalSHA256": "6c52996f6914ba2d6d0e068c70b58c1d69617bfe225fa9fe8fb8b65959c5f804",
          "primaryGround": "Te Papa L43 states that, when plates are changed, the printing blanket is wiped with solvent to remove any trace of the old image. This asks that changeover function, distinct from generic equipment identity and the blanket-to-paper transfer method.",
          "locator": "L43; full changeover context L38-44",
          "sourcePaths": [
            {
              "path": "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/process-v2-books-remaining10-fresh-source-01a14018/author/sources/tepapa-how-books-printed.html",
              "url": "https://blog.tepapa.govt.nz/2016/11/18/how-are-books-printed/",
              "sha256": "e20ffd4339dbb362a99ee0cd7b6bc83586bb6e52e53296c150381e12a997d0c3",
              "type": "complete captured HTML"
            },
            {
              "path": "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/process-v2-books-remaining10-fresh-source-01a14018/author/sources/tepapa-how-books-printed.readable.txt",
              "url": "https://blog.tepapa.govt.nz/2016/11/18/how-are-books-printed/",
              "sha256": "588a7b199acb02568ad2563f8ef0a9e51db582f59036e776d50dd8f370db4d9c",
              "type": "complete captured readable body"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "explanation",
          "literal": "После смены форм резиновое полотно протирают растворителем, чтобы убрать след старого изображения. Затем печатник запускает пробные листы и проверяет качество настройки.",
          "literalSHA256": "94837440c617444c73face2da7d2834c238c463ae04ee074faa18ed1cd8f1b49",
          "primaryGround": "The source states the purpose of solvent-cleaning the blanket during plate changes: remove the previous image trace. L44 then describes test sheets and quality checks after changeover.",
          "locator": "L43-44",
          "sourcePaths": [
            {
              "path": "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/process-v2-books-remaining10-fresh-source-01a14018/author/sources/tepapa-how-books-printed.html",
              "url": "https://blog.tepapa.govt.nz/2016/11/18/how-are-books-printed/",
              "sha256": "e20ffd4339dbb362a99ee0cd7b6bc83586bb6e52e53296c150381e12a997d0c3",
              "type": "complete captured HTML"
            },
            {
              "path": "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/process-v2-books-remaining10-fresh-source-01a14018/author/sources/tepapa-how-books-printed.readable.txt",
              "url": "https://blog.tepapa.govt.nz/2016/11/18/how-are-books-printed/",
              "sha256": "588a7b199acb02568ad2563f8ef0a9e51db582f59036e776d50dd8f370db4d9c",
              "type": "complete captured readable body"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note0",
          "literal": "На углах листа сверяют приводочные метки: они показывают, точно ли наложены цветовые формы.",
          "literalSHA256": "e74f231ddea250bfb9eabaf6884dc68d1a2640551d6579a355c07de0bcd83bec",
          "primaryGround": "Te Papa L29 describes registration marks at sheet corners being checked so all four colour plates are precisely superimposed.",
          "locator": "L29",
          "sourcePaths": [
            {
              "path": "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/process-v2-books-remaining10-fresh-source-01a14018/author/sources/tepapa-how-books-printed.html",
