      "absoluteDifficulty": {
        "level": "easy",
        "status": "PASS",
        "audienceGround": "The keyed relation is an ordinary reason to wipe a surface during a changeover: remove traces of the prior image. The prompt supplies the press context; no specialized term or multistep printing knowledge is needed to distinguish this from registration, ink adjustment, or curing."
      },
      "mainDistinctness": {
        "status": "PASS",
        "reason": "The old main asked which machine repeatedly prints on a sheet or roll, overlapping journalism-news rotary-printing machinery. This prompt asks the specific cleaning purpose at plate changeover. It does not test the paper page material (order55), ink as colorant (56), or the blanket transfer method named by offset-process."
      }
